{#
    One card, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property.** The directive says what the card is — the
    title, where it goes, the kind, the label, the picture — and each of those
    lands on `sds-card` as an attribute. Nothing here says what a card looks
    like: not the frame, not the row above the title, not what a title is
    wrapped in. That is the whole point of there being a component. This
    template used to spell `.sds-card__body` and `.sds-card__title` because the
    element read its own parts back to find them, which made every internal name
    public API and left the element framing markup this file had already built —
    a card that could not be changed on one side without the other.

    What paid for that arrangement was the reader with no JavaScript, and it is
    not needed any more: `make guides` renders every element in the output ahead
    of the browser — `scripts/lib/prerender.ts` — so a property reaches a page
    that runs no script at all.

    The body is the one thing still written between the tags, because it is the
    one thing an attribute cannot hold: out of a document it is paragraphs, and
    sometimes a list.

    The title is where TYPO3 documentation puts the target: `.. card::
    :ref:`Installation <installation>``. So the words of it are the heading and
    the reference is where the card goes, and the element decides what a title
    is wrapped in and how far the link reaches — which is over the whole card.
    `:href:` is the same thing said as a path, and wins where both are written.
#}
{#- The picture goes by the name every other directive that takes a file uses:
    what an option is called belongs to the language it is written in, and
    `.. figure::` and `.. image::` already gave the file that name.

    Resolved here and not in the element: what a path means is the renderer's
    business — which document it was written in, and whether it points out of
    the site — and the element is handed the URL that came of it. -#}
{%- set src = node.option('src') -%}
{%- set source = src ? (src is external_target ? src : asset(src)) : '' -%}
{%- set href = node.option('href') ? renderLink(node.option('href')) : linkUrl(node.link) -%}
<sds-card
    heading="{{ node.title.toString }}"
    {%- if href %} href="{{ href }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('label') %} label="{{ node.option('label') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('tag') %} tag="{{ node.option('tag') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('icon') %} icon="{{ node.option('icon') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if source %} src="{{ source }}" alt="{{ node.option('alt')|default('') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('footer') %} footer="{{ node.option('footer') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('action') %} action="{{ node.option('action') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}
>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-card>
